    kg:text """backgroundsand depictionsofhumansandanimals.

Wethenincorporatesecondary colorsto highlightand differentiatevariouselements.These colors representthings slikedifferent typesof diseases or group elements,and create distinctionswithin the illustrations.Thisensures s thatourillustrations aren't justinformative,but are alsovisually organized andeasy tounderstand.

Pleaserefer to thededicated'Color'chapterforthecorrectcolor codestoensureprecise color representation.

<!-- image -->

Symptom depictionsandmagnifyingtheissue

Use secondary colors exclusively for'Symptom depictions'on animal fur and human clothing. Use white for all otherbodyrepresentations,whether human or animal.

Various shades of gray are used for depicting the organs,using a darker gray outline for clarity. The specific illnessarea is highlightedwithsecondary colors.

<!-- image -->""" ;
