<urn:kg:boehringer-ingelheim:section:3865db89-18be-4f89-b00f-b3028acee091> a kg:Section ;
    rdfs:label "Introduction - Imagery.pdf" ;
    kg:SECTION_HAS_CHUNK <urn:kg:boehringer-ingelheim:chunk:44538969-69dc-461c-8394-e4d028ef0381>,
        <urn:kg:boehringer-ingelheim:chunk:497796c4-3a83-42f2-8feb-1e11915c4cf5> ;
    kg:extraction_method "docling" ;
    kg:graphScope "brand" ;
    kg:page_number 5 ;
    kg:section_id "3865db89-18be-4f89-b00f-b3028acee091" ;
    kg:section_title "Our style criteria" ;
    kg:section_type "heading" ;
    kg:source_document_id "ded4ae29-e5c0-417b-8c08-00855d252370" ;
    kg:source_document_type "guidance_document" ;
    kg:source_file_name "Introduction - Imagery.pdf" ;
    kg:text """To choose or create new imagery, we use the following criteria:

Free composition

<!-- image -->

Thisis aboutcapturinglivelyimages.Ourimagessharedynamic perspectives and asymmetricalcomposition.

Avoid:symmetricalor centered static compositions.

<!-- image -->

We create depth.Thishappens organically/randomlywhen we

Spatial depth capturepeopleingroups.

Avoid: any subjects being in a staged formation.

<!-- image -->

<!-- image -->

No eye contact

Wedocumentreallife,sotakepositionofanobserver.Wewant subject/stobeunawareofeachshot.Exception:wedon'texpect you to creatively direct an animal!So,it's ok if animals look into the camera naturally.

Avoid:directeyecontactwiththe camera,asit willfeel staged.

<!-- image -->

We choose dynamicimages.Oursubjects should bemoving naturally,spontaneously and engaging inrealactivities.Exception: people are allowed to stand and be still,as long as they are engaged

Portraymovement in a task.

Avoid:staged andstaticsubjects.

<!-- image -->

<!-- image -->

<!-- image -->

Immersion Wedocumentreality asif the audienceis fullyimmersedinthesceneandfeelspart of it.

<!-- image -->

Chance

Wechoosesurpriseand chanceovera perfectcomposition-that'swhywe capturethespontaneousand unplanned moments.

<!-- image -->

<!-- image -->""" .

