    kg:source_document_type "brand_book" ;
    kg:source_file_name "BI Design Style Guide 1.pdf" ;
    kg:text """InSceneillustrations,wewant to tella storyorcreate aspecific atmosphere.Secondary colors achieve this bygiving us abroaderspectrum of hues.This then helpsus evokespecificemotions and create a playful look andfeel.

When changing thecolor,it'sessential thatthebackground seamlesslyintegrateswith the colorsof the

illustration.

Asageneralrule,alwaysselect colorsthatoptimizelegibilityand create a defined contrast.We alsoneed to minimizethedifferenceinvibrancybetweencolors.

Head to the dedicated'Color'chapterforthe correctcolorcodestoensureprecise colorrepresentation.

<!-- image -->

"Warm Gray'background

<!-- image -->

Violetbackground

Fromlighttomediumshades

Bluebackground Fromlight tomedium shades

<!-- image -->

Red background Fromlighttomediumshades

<!-- image -->

Please ensure thatonlyprofessionals(designers and illustrators) handle comprehensive edits to Sceneillustrations.

Note: Don't use'Dark Green'or'Accent Green'asa background color for Scene illustrations.""" .

